abstract: >-
  Reference implementation, kernels, benchmark drivers and result files for the technical
  report on co-activation permuted block sparsity: a functionally isomorphic 32-lane permutation
  of the FFN intermediate dimension, a cross-layer adaptive energy budget instead of a fixed
  Top-K, and block-major 4.5-bit storage that makes DRAM traffic scale with the skip rate.
  The report separates what the mechanism buys from where hardware limits stop it.
keywords:
  - transformer inference
  - block sparsity
  - activation sparsity
  - AVX-512
  - CUDA
  - quantisation
  - cache-line alignment
